# Project Scope

FCHIP frontend is the Flutter client for the Community Health Intelligence Platform, against the `fchip-backend` API. Product boundaries: [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../../.cursor/app-write-up.mdc).

## Mandatory rules

- Must build production-ready workspaces aligned with the FCHIP SoT, not a generic disconnected starter.
- Must support Android, iOS, Web, Windows, macOS, and Linux where enabled; extra-small mobile through large desktop; smartwatch out of scope.
- Must integrate with `fchip-backend` via repositories and DTOs; HTTP details live in `backend/.cursor/api.mdc` and `network_api.mdc`.
- Should prefer Flutter SDK widgets, Material Design, and shared `lib/shared/` abstractions before custom packages.
- Must not duplicate dependencies, folders, components, rules, and competing design systems.
- Menus, routes, forms, actions, and visibility must match backend permissions, entitlements, and APIs.
- Must reference entities by `human_friendly_id`; backend maps internal IDs.
- Must enforce RBAC+ABAC and subscription-package intersection ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).

## Architecture invariants

- One architecture, one routing system (`go_router`), one state system (Riverpod), one design system, one shared component strategy.
- Mutation/reconciliation is owned by [`instant_ui_sync.mdc`](./instant_ui_sync.mdc); layer boundaries by [`architecture.mdc`](./architecture.mdc).

## Minimum runnable contract

- Startup: `main.dart`, `bootstrap.dart`, provider scope, predictable flow.
- Shell: `MaterialApp.router`, `go_router`, not-found route, responsive shell with menu bar and collapsible side nav.
- Theme: Material 3 light/dark/system with shared tokens.
- State: Riverpod with override-ready boundaries.
- Localization: English ARB baseline, `l10n.yaml`, generated l10n.
- Workspaces: `AppWorkspace` + `AppListTable` ([`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc)).

